# HIL run (tools/pps/hil, #37, #434), limit: 20 forced light sleeps in a row are all survived (`boot` says place 10) and crashes.txt has no more entries than before the flash (run.sh gives --baseline: the count read before it). The run is on USB with sleep 0, so nothing else would ever sleep lightly.
test:05-crashes {
  repeat:20 {
    nap:3
  }
  crashes
  assert:crashes.count<=baseline:no new crashes
}
